 "answer": "NO -- the perturbation is a property of the whole pre-cutover half, not of the 24 days. Under the SH/SZ union, 357 changes on a median 69.4% of securities on the 396 days that never broke the floor versus 73.9% on the 24 that did, and 471 on 64.8% versus 65.2%. The worst-perturbed pre-cutover days by 357 rank correlation are not problem days at all (min 0.8825 on a non-problem day vs 0.9704 worst among problem days). Coverage gain does differ (634 labels/day on problem days vs 545 elsewhere), but the 396 non-problem days still gain 400-657 labels each, so the union rewrites the pre-cutover segment everywhere.",
